   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_gpio.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   *          functionalities of the GPIO peripheral:           
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   *           + GPIO Read and Write
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   *           + GPIO Alternate functions configuration
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   * 
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c **** @verbatim  
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****  ===============================================================================
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                       ##### How to use this driver #####
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****  ===============================================================================       
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****  [..]             
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) Enable the GPIO AHB clock using the following function
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        RCC_AHB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_AHB1Periph_GPIOx, ENABLE);
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) Configure the GPIO pin(s) using GPIO_Init()
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        Four possible configuration are available for each pin:
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        (++) Input: Floating, Pull-up, Pull-down.
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        (++) Output: Push-Pull (Pull-up, Pull-down or no Pull)
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             Open Drain (Pull-up, Pull-down or no Pull). In output mode, the speed 
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             is configurable: 2 MHz, 25 MHz, 50 MHz or 100 MHz.
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        (++) Alternate Function: Push-Pull (Pull-up, Pull-down or no Pull) Open 
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             Drain (Pull-up, Pull-down or no Pull).
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        (++) Analog: required mode when a pin is to be used as ADC channel or DAC 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccPcbn3J.s 			page 2


  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             output.
  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) Peripherals alternate function:
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        (++) For ADC and DAC, configure the desired pin in analog mode using 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             GPIO_InitStruct->GPIO_Mode = GPIO_Mode_AN;
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             (+++) For other peripherals (TIM, USART...):
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             (+++) Connect the pin to the desired peripherals' Alternate 
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                      Function (AF) using GPIO_PinAFConfig() function
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             (+++) Configure the desired pin in alternate function mode using
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                      GPIO_InitStruct->GPIO_Mode = GPIO_Mode_AF
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             (+++) Select the type, pull-up/pull-down and output speed via 
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                      GPIO_PuPd, GPIO_OType and GPIO_Speed members
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             (+++) Call GPIO_Init() function
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****           
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) To get the level of a pin configured in input mode use GPIO_ReadInputDataBit()
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****             
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) To set/reset the level of a pin configured in output mode use 
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        GPIO_SetBits()/GPIO_ResetBits()
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                  
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) During and just after reset, the alternate functions are not 
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        active and the GPIO pins are configured in input floating mode (except JTAG
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        pins).
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) The LSE oscillator pins OSC32_IN and OSC32_OUT can be used as general purpose 
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        (PC14 and PC15, respectively) when the LSE oscillator is off. The LSE has 
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        priority over the GPIO function.
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****    (#) The HSE oscillator pins OSC_IN/OSC_OUT can be used as 
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        general purpose PH0 and PH1, respectively, when the HSE oscillator is off. 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****        The HSE has priority over the GPIO function.
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****                
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c **** @endverbatim        
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   *
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_gpio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
